`set_property` first normalizes `value` inside a `try` around `next(iter(value))` for non-strings. For `[]`, iterating succeeds but `next(...)` raises `StopIteration`, which is caught by the first handler. For `12345`, `iter(value)` fails because an integer is not iterable, so `TypeError` is caught by the second handler. Then the X11 update call is wrapped in `except xcffib.xproto.WindowError`; the test patches that name to `_DummyWindowError`, and only the third `.check()` raises, so `_DummyWindowError` is the final caught exception kind.

